Description:

An incoming iTIP scheduling message (delivered by iMIP email through the Sieve
processcalendar/processimip action, or through the CalDAV scheduling inbox) is
now merged safely when it carries more than one VTIMEZONE that shares a single
TZID.  Previously the merge freed the stored timezone component the first time
a TZID matched but left it in its lookup table, so a second VTIMEZONE with the
same TZID freed the same component again, corrupting the heap and crashing the
delivery worker.


